{
  "rationale": "Evidence from iteration 6 (score 680.02, essentially level with iteration 5 at 680.31). Raising kd from 2.0 to 2.5 gave a small oval gain (mean time 2.08 s, oscillation 0.11) and held s-bend at 20 of 20 finishes, but slalom did not change: 0 of 20 finishes, 20 off-track exits, progress 0.42 (down from 0.50). So kd is near its useful limit and is no longer the binding constraint. The remaining failure is leaving the tape at sharp direction changes on the slalom. Iteration 5 showed that a larger footprint reduced line loss there, and the sensor array still covers only ±0.06 m, which is the coverage limit that matters at large offsets.\n\nChanges, kept to two levers so the effect can be read:\n(1) Geometry: move from 5 to 7 line sensors spread across the full allowed width, x = -0.075, -0.05, -0.025, 0, 0.025, 0.05, 0.075 m at y = 0.08 m. This means the robot still sees the tape at larger lateral offsets before it leaves the track, and it gives finer signal resolution on the slalom's direction changes. Sensor size stays 0.016 m, and mass 0.5 kg, wheel_track 0.10 m and wheel_radius 0.03 m are unchanged.\n(2) Controller: sensor weights become proportional to x with a slope of about 26.7 per metre, giving -2, -1.33, -0.67, 0, 0.67, 1.33, 2. This keeps the signal within the ±2 limit at the outer sensors. The slope is lower than before (about 33), so kp rises from 5.5 to 6.0 to keep the steering gain per metre of offset close to the previous level. kd stays at 2.5, base_speed at 1.0, ki at 0, and line_loss at last_direction.\n\nExpected result: slalom line-loss events fall, and slalom progress rises above 0.5 with some completions. Oval and s-bend should hold at or near their current finish rates. Hypotheses: H1, wider sensor coverage at the outer edge reduces off-track exits on the slalom, shown by line_loss_events falling below 0.75 and max_error staying under 0.06 on more seeds. H2, the lower signal slope with kp 6.0 keeps the steering response similar on the oval and s-bend, shown by oval mean time near 2.1 s and s-bend finishes at or above 19 of 20. H3, if steering_oscillation rises above 0.3 on the slalom, the extra sensors are adding noise to the signal and kp should come back toward 5.5. Next measurements: progress and completion_time for speed versus stability, max_error and line_loss_events for stability, steering_oscillation for damping, control_effort for gain cost, and noise_robustness for margin on the held-back tracks.",
